ORBIT
A memory that keeps circling because it never resolved

Duration: 25 seconds
Aspect Ratio: 9:16 (vertical)
FPS: 48
Color: Black & white, high micro-contrast, soft halation on highlights
Grain: Fine analog film grain, constant, subtle
Tone Arc: Tender → uncanny → inevitable
Rule: No additional people appear beyond the two figures. No cuts to other locations.

CORE RULES (LOCKED)

❌ NO STATIC FRAMES
❌ NO CAMERA LOCK
❌ NO FULL FACE ALIGNMENT
❌ NO DRAMATIC EVENTS

✅ Camera always in motion (orbital drift minimum)
✅ The moon rotates continuously
✅ Camera counter-rotates at a different rate
✅ Motion must feel remembered, not observed
✅ Loop-safe ending (end can cut to start seamlessly)

WORLD LOGIC (LOCKED)
The moon is not celestial — it is a mechanism of memory
The couple is not moving around the moon
→ they are moving with it
The world below repeats because it cannot progress
Time slips slightly each rotation
Gravity is stable but negotiated
Nothing resolves; nothing breaks

CAMERA LANGUAGE
POV-adjacent, intimate but detached
Macro-scale lens feel (shallow depth, exaggerated parallax)
Subtle handheld inertia, as if the camera is breathing
Focus breathes gently, never snaps
Rotation mismatch between subject and background is essential

SEQUENCE TIMELINE
0–4s
Slow orbital drift begins
Moon rotates clockwise
Camera counter-rotates slower, counter-clockwise
Their hands hover close but never touch
Background architecture softly parallax-shifts

4–9s
Rotation continues
Tiny background elements below repeat in slightly different positions
Micro time smear appears on edges of motion
Their faces approach alignment… then miss by millimeters

9–14s
Loop anomaly emerges:
The same structure below passes twice
Dust falls upward briefly, then resumes normal behavior
Fabric folds ripple like geological layers
Camera drifts closer, never frontal

14–19s
Orbital rhythm becomes hypnotic
Subtle ghosting trails appear during rotation
Moon surface texture shifts — craters don’t move consistently
Their proximity tightens, but alignment is still denied

19–23s
Camera passes partially behind the moon
Sound thins
Rotation rates nearly sync, then deliberately desync again
One near-touch moment — fingers almost meet

23–25s
Camera clears the moon
Composition matches opening frame almost exactly
A single detail is wrong (dust position / shadow angle)

24.5 - 25.0
Cut mid-motion for perfect loop
ends cleanly


SOUND DESIGN
Low-frequency hum (felt more than heard)
Stone-on-stone micro clicks
Very soft rotational whoosh
No dialogue, only FX, SFX, and Background Music

Silence is active, not empty

FINAL INTENT

This is not a love scene.
This is a system keeping love in motion so it never has to end.

